WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.200
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
everybody.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.734
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.734
Well, guys, today is Earth Day.

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:07.200
Today is Earth Day.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.968
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.734
Yeah, everyone is trying
to do their part.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:13.834
As we speak,
CNN is properly disposing

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:16.767
of CNN+.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:17.968
In honor of Earth Day,

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:20.434
I saw that President Biden
visited Seattle

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:24.901
and signed an executive order
to safeguard old-growth forests.

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:27.300
That's great. Can we see
an old-growth forest?

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.400
[ Laughter and applause ]
Oh, look at that chest hair.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.100
Yeah, that's nice.
Look at that chest hair.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.634
-Ooh la la.
-[ French accent ] Oh, am I

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:32.701
sexy enough for you?

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:34.167
[ Laughter ]
Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.467
While Biden was in Seattle,

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:38.767
he also spoke about the need
for using clean energy

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:41.133
and he even demonstrated
how powerful windmills can be.

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.167
Watch this.

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:45.534
[ Whirring ]

00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:46.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:47.601
Yeah.

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:50.367
Oh, there you go.
They are powerful.

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:52.200
Ahead of Earth Day,

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.934
Apple announced that it is using
more recycled materials

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:57.567
to make its products
than ever before.

00:00:57.567 --> 00:00:59.033
Yeah, recycled iPhones.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:01.467
It's weird when you turn on your
new iPhone and Siri says --

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:03.100
-I used to be a Shake Weight.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.000
-Okay.
I don't know.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.367
Guys, the second weekend
of Coachella just kicked off

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.267
and I heard that,
since the first weekend,

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:15.968
COVID cases in the area
have gone up by 77%.

00:01:15.968 --> 00:01:17.067
[ Oohs and ohs ]

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:18.567
Everyone there is like,
"I can't believe

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.734
this is happening
when we're doing everything

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:22.100
we're not supposed to do!"

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:28.367
Meanwhile, with all the news
about shifting mask guidelines,

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:30.067
it's time to play the game
that's sweeping the nation...

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:36.200
♪♪
[ Applause ]

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.133
This is the game where we pick
a random audience member

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:41.968
and guess if there's a stache

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:45.000
[ Laughter and applause ]
under their mask.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.267
So please welcome tonight's
audience member, Kevin Sproul.

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:49.334
Kevin, where are you?

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:51.033
♪♪

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:54.033
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:58.400
♪♪

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.501
Nice to see you, Kevin.

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:02.868
Kevin, thank you for being
on "The Tonight Show."

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:03.934
Kevin, where are you from?

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.767
-San Diego.
-San Diego.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.200
That's all I can ask you.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.501
[ Laughter ]
Alright, now, we have

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:11.934
to figure out if you've got
a stache under that mask.

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:12.834
Wait, hold on.

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:13.767
Quest, you go first.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.234
You can ask him one question

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.901
and then you must
make your guess.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.567
-Alright.
-Think hard.

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:21.234
You only get one.
-I got one.

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:26.200
-Okay. Kevin. Okay.
-Okay, so, at dinner,

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.033
how many napkins
are you likely to use?

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:30.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:33.467
I'm actually an exceptionally
clean eater,

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:36.701
so I usually
only use one napkin.

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:38.400
-Mm.
Tricky.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.300
[ Murmuring ]

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.934
[ Laughter ]
Mm.

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:43.667
-Are you going to guess now?

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:45.033
Or are you going to save it?

00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:47.133
-Oh, okay.
I'll guess now.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.000
I think he has a stache.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.434
I think he's trying to trap me.

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:52.400
-Okay. Okay.
He said one napkin. Okay.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.934
Higgins, your turn.
What's your question?

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:54.634
-Hmm.

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:58.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:00.434
-San Diego, again?
-San Diego.

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:01.834
-San Diego, California?

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:03.701
-Indeed.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:05.067
-Got it.
That's my question.

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:06.434
-That almost counts
as a question.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:09.434
That can't be your question.
Is San Diego in California

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:10.667
is the question.
-Is it in California?

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:11.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:14.234
Does it take you, now,
the same amount of time

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:16.300
as it always has to shave?

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.167
-Yes.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:23.100
-Pff!
I'm going to say

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.167
no stache.

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:26.801
-Yeah!
-Yeah. Okay.

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.868
Okay. Okay. My turn.

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:30.234
-It's in California.

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:31.634
-Thank you.
No, that's not my question.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:34.868
[ Laughter ]
Okay. Okay.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:36.100
San Diego.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.067
You look like
a clean-cut dude to me.

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.968
Alright, here's my question.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:45.100
Do people mistake you for

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.901
Burt Reynolds
or Timothée Chalamet?

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:49.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:52.234
-I would say the most I get is

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:53.334
the Buddha.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:54.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.067
-Ah!

00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:57.300
-Buddha was cleanshaven.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.367
Buddha is cleanshaven,
is what I think.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:03.267
You say no stache.
-I say no stache.

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:04.834
-Quest?
-I say stache.

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:06.701
-You say stache.
-Yes.

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:09.133
-Gosh! I'm getting this vibe
of no stache.

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:10.601
I think he's a clean-cut dude.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:11.801
I think no stache.

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:12.968
It's time to find out...

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:16.734
-...is there a stache
under that mask?

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:18.501
[ Drumroll ]

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:19.634
-Ah!

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:22.033
[ Rimshot ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:23.501
Oh.

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:25.267
That's not bad. Thank you, man.
I appreciate it.

00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:27.601
Oh, wait, Kevin!
I'm sorry.

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:29.767
Thank you for playing.
Of course, here,

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:32.100
you've won a two-week supply
of Turtle Wax.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.367
[ Laughter and applause ]
-There you go.
-Turtle Wax.

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:36.234
When you're here, you're family.

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:37.634
[ Laughter ]
Thank you for playing, bud.

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:39.834
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:41.868
Wow!
Stache.

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:44.167
[ Rimshot ]

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:45.868
-He knew. He knew.
-Yeah, looks good,

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.968
looks good, looks good.

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:50.334
Alright, anyways,
getting back to the news.

00:04:50.334 --> 00:04:52.868
Well, guys, the Tony Awards
are coming up

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:56.367
and they just issued
a strict no-violence policy...

00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:57.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.734 --> 00:04:59.501
...to potential ticket buyers.

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.234
That's right, the Tonys,
no violence.

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:05.133
No violence, yeah.
Because you can always tell

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:06.400
a fight's going to break out
at the Tonys

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.734
when people start snapping.

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:09.133
[ Snapping fingers ]
♪♪

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:10.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:11.467
♪ Hey, boy ♪

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:15.501
♪♪

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:16.567
I appreciate it.

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:19.767
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:21.701
Water?

00:05:21.701 --> 00:05:22.534
-Oxygen?

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:23.767
-Some business news --

00:05:23.767 --> 00:05:27.501
I read that the CEO of Old Navy
is stepping down.

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:29.801
Now, Old Navy's going to try on
a dozen new CEOs

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:31.033
before finding one that fits

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:32.300
and leaving the rest
on the floor.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.334
[ Laughter and applause ]
It's very interesting.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.033
And, finally, this weekend,

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:39.834
two stunt pilots will attempt
the first ever plane swap.

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:41.467
This is where they're going
to fly close together,

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:42.968
go into a nosedive,

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:45.434
then jump into each other's
planes before landing.

00:05:45.434 --> 00:05:47.634
[ Laughter and ohs ]
Yeah, it'll be the one time

00:05:47.634 --> 00:05:49.200
the pilot
actually deserves applause

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.400
for landing the plane.
There you go.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.467
[ Laughter and applause ]
We have a great show.

